          "title": "Why Are We Still Reading a 2,400-Year-Old Manual?",
          "content": "In 350 BCE, a balding Greek philosopher named **Aristotle** sat down to figure out why some speakers move audiences to tears, action, or revolt while others empty a room.\n\nHe wrote **Rhetoric** — and almost every speech you've ever admired (MLK at the Lincoln Memorial, Steve Jobs at Stanford, your favorite TED Talk) is still running on his operating system.\n\nThis lesson is the foundation of everything else in this course. Master the **rhetorical triangle**, the **canons of rhetoric**, and the **rhetorical situation**, and you'll stop guessing why some speeches work — you'll engineer them on purpose.",
