          "explanation": "Great data slide titles **carry the takeaway**, not the topic. Option C tells the audience EXACTLY what to see in the chart before they look. The audience's eye then confirms — not investigates. Options A, B, and D are topic-labels that force the audience to figure out the point themselves. This is the **Cole Nussbaumer principle** of titles: if your chart title doesn't tell me what to see, your chart isn't ready to show.",
