          "explanation": "The most impactful single change: **takeaway-title + highlight-the-one-thing-that-matters + direct-label-not-legend**. Option B applies three reinforcing principles at once: title carries meaning, the audience's eye goes immediately to the highlighted data, and direct labels eliminate the legend-hunting tax. More colors (A) makes things harder. 3D effects (C) destroy data-ink ratio. Adding a paragraph (D) triggers the redundancy principle — text + spoken explanation = overload. The Tufte / Nussbaumer principle: cut decoration, highlight the point.",
