          "explanation": "Every lesson in this course has reinforced ONE throughline: **public speaking is a learnable, lifelong practice grounded in audience-first thinking, deliberate craft, and exposure**. Aristotle gave us the architecture. Stage fright is hackable. Audience analysis comes first. Message has structure. Openings and closings are engineered. Body and voice are trainable. Slides have rules. Persuasion is a journey. Special occasions have formulas. And the only path forward is deliberate practice. Talent is overrated. Mechanical canons are necessary but insufficient. Charisma is a SYMPTOM of craft, not its cause.",
